# Sphinx of Forgotten Lore: "Flash" (CR 702.8a) and "Flying" (CR 702.9b), from its Oracle text. Bot1 Bolts Bot2 on turn 1, then casts the
# Sphinx in Bot2's turn-2 end step (Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire), which only flash allows. Attacking on turn 3, its trigger gives the Bolt
# flashback; Bot2's Memnite, which has neither flying nor reach, cannot block it. After combat Bot1 flashes back the Bolt for {R}: Bot2 is at
# 20 - 3 - 3 - 3 = 11 and the Bolt is exiled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Sphinx of Forgotten Lore
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sphinx of Forgotten Lore.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sphinx of Forgotten Lore.Keywords = Flash; Flying
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Sphinx of Forgotten Lore > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Block(Memnite > Sphinx of Forgotten Lore)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 11
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite
Exile = Lightning Bolt
